# Toyota Corolla E120 five-door hatchback, 2002-2007.
#
# The ninth-generation Corolla. UK launch 2 January 2002; the British hatchbacks
# were built at Burnaston and took about 55 per cent of launch sales in
# five-door form against 20 per cent for the three-door. The hatchbacks were
# replaced by the Auris on 1 February 2007; the Corolla name left the British
# range in 2008.
# https://media.toyota.co.uk/teed-up-for-success-the-new-toyota-corolla/
# https://media.toyota.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/sites/5/pdf/Corolla-gen9-UK-launch-pack-2002.pdf
# https://media.toyota.co.uk/auris-the-new-toyota/
#
# Dimensions 4.180 x 1.705 x 1.470 m, wheelbase 2.600 m. Source: English
# Wikipedia, "Toyota Corolla (E120)" infobox: wheelbase 2,600 mm; hatchback
# length 4,180 mm; width 1,705 mm for 2004-07 cars; height 1,460-1,486 mm
# across the US sedan trims, and 1.470 m is used, the European hatchback
# figure. The fitted model is 4.181 m long, 1.705 m wide, 1.470 m high, with
# the wheel centres 2.600 m apart (62.2 per cent of length). Mirrors take the
# modelled width to 2.018 m.
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is a shallow front-left oblique rather than a level
# elevation (the grille and plate are visible and the near front wheel is
# larger), so the model was compared at that angle and a separate true
# elevation was rendered for coherence. Image 1 supplied the long roof, the
# waistline and the arches; image 2 the 2004-onward facelift nose; image 3 the
# hatch and tall corner lamps, from the rear right; image 4 corroborated the
# nose only. The five-door hatchback is the body modelled.
#
# Colours are Toyota GB names from the 2003 brochure, evidence grade (a):
# Pure White, Sunburst Red, Lunar Shadow, Lucerne Silver, Igneous Grey (T Sport
# only), Thunder Grey, Eclipse Black, Island Green, Carlo Blue and Neptune
# Blue. Four common British finishes are modelled: Lucerne Silver, Pure White,
# Eclipse Black and Sunburst Red. Weights silver 3, white 3, red 2, black 2,
# total 10, provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 185 km/h, the 1.6-litre car's quoted maximum. Comfort 95/473, on the
# line 330 + 1.5 x 95: a roomy, quiet family hatchback, the best of the three
# Corolla generations built here. Classes 0,1.
#
# Dates are road presence: January 2002 intro, retires staggered 2015-2018 on a
# thirteen- to sixteen-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/toyota-corolla-e120.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/toyota-corolla-e120.dae (55 objects). References:
# citycars/references/toyota-corolla-e120/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the front bumper is squarer, the headlamps more faceted
# and the door seams less distinct than the photographs. The top view confirms
# a continuous painted roof and the windscreen is visible from the front. At
# 128 px the tall body, the long roof and the steep hatch read as the
# ninth-generation Corolla.

obj=citycar
